SARkit is a suite of Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR)-related tools in Python
developed and maintained by Valkyrie Systems Corporation to encourage the use of
National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) SAR data standards.

With SARkit, you can:
- read and write SAR standards files (CRSD, CPHD, SICD, SIDD)
- interact with SAR XML metadata using more convenient Python objects
- check SAR data/metadata files for inconsistencies

This project was developed as the modern successor to SarPy.
